<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lucterius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lucterius was a leader of the Cadurci in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> and one of the chief commanders in the Gallic revolt of 52 BCE under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vercingetorix">Vercingetorix</a>, when he raised the peoples of the south against the Roman Province. In 51 BCE he and the Senonian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drappes">Drappes</a> held Uxellodunum against Caesar. He escaped the siege but was later handed over to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> by the Arvernian Epasnactus.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lucterius.jpg" alt="Lucterius" width="320" height="330" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Publication de la Société des lettres, sciences et arts de la Corrèze (Tulle) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lucterios_m%C3%A9daille_du_mon%C3%A9taire_Sasserna.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
